LOCK                                                           [3.0]
----

Format:      LOCK [d: [ON | OFF]]

Purpose:     Locks or unlocks a drive.

Use:         If no parameters are given,  then the drives  that  are
        currently locked are listed.

             If  only a drive is given,  then the lock state of that
        drive is displayed.

             If ON or OFF is also given,  then the drive  is  locked
        or unlocked appropriately.

             While a drive is locked,  Nextor assumes that the  disk
        or storage device mapped to it never changes,  and skips the
        media change checks that are otherwise performed every  time
        the  drive  is  accessed.  This  speeds  up  access  to  the
        removable devices (such as SD cards or USB storage) that are
        used as fixed storage.  Locking a drive whose media  is then
        actually changed can corrupt the new disk, so use with care.

             The lock is released automatically when a disk error on
        the drive is aborted.

Examples:

        LOCK
        No drives are locked

             No  parameters  were given,  so the locked  drives  are
        listed; in this case no drive was locked.

        LOCK B: ON

             Drive B: is locked.

        LOCK B:
        B: is locked

             Only a drive was given, so its lock state is printed.
